@startuml
title GET /api/ai-agents-teams/grants/by-grantor/{address} and /grants/by-grantee/{address}
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Grantor UI /\nchannel operator" as Caller #FFD8C2
participant "AgentsTeamsApiSdk\n.grantsByGrantor() /\n.grantsByGrantee(addr)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "Observer\n(exploratory read)" as Obs #FFF1CC

Caller -> SDK : list grants
SDK -> API : GET .../grants/by-grantor/{address}\nor .../grants/by-grantee/{address}
API -> Domain : list grants
Domain -> Obs : render listGrantsByGrantor /\nlistGrantsByGrantee; exploratory deploy\n(costs nothing, finalizes nothing)
Obs -> Obs : filterEntriesByField over the public\ngrants map: grantor == addr /\ngrantee == addr
Obs --> Domain : [grant records]
Domain --> API : [Grant] — revoked grants included, flagged
API --> SDK : 200 [Grant]
SDK --> Caller : rows for the management table /\nrouting cache refresh

note over SDK, Obs #FFF0C7
Grant records are PUBLIC authorization facts: no secrets
travel here (require_token exists on chain only as its
blake2b-256 digest). Channel services consume the
observer-readable chain clauses directly — chain-read-first —
and use these HTTP mirrors for UI and diagnostics; a stale
answer costs one failed paid deploy, never a wrong
authorization, because the chain re-adjudicates at claim time.
end note
@enduml
